@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Limbs of sections that pass 1 encoded in part: Gov. Code § 6700(b), § 6801 (the first day of the year), § 6808(a) and (c), § 9606 (second sentence) and
-- § 16.5(d), (e), (f).
--
-- Added in pass 2 of the completion to "whole".  Pass 1 left these limbs out or called them inert because they compute nothing from a date; the brief allows
-- `inert` only for a provision that is not operative, is machinery, or is shown repealed or blank, and each of these is operative.  Each is encoded here as what it says.
-- The quotation lines are copied by script from the converter-made plain-text rendering of the sections (not the official text) and checked against it by srcrefs.py.
-- Target: unstable (REFUSE).  Imports: prelude and daydate (for YMD).
--
-- The other deposited codes that these limbs cite are not deposited: the Civil Code § 1633.2(h) definition of "electronic signature", the Public Resources Code,
-- 15 U.S.C. §§ 261 and 263, and the Uniform Electronic Transactions Act.  Whatever turns on them is a fact the caller supplies, or a named REFUSE.

§ `Gov. Code § 6700(b): a memorandum of understanding that conflicts with the holiday section`

-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:31 | (b) If this section is in conflict with the provisions of a memorandum of understanding reached pursuant to Chapter 12 (commencing with Section 3560) of Division 4 of Title 1, the memorandum of understanding shall be controlling without further legislative action, except that if those provisions of a memorandum of understanding require the expenditure of funds, the provisions shall not become effective unless approved by the Legislature in the annual Budget Act.
@ref Gov. Code § 6700(b) (src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:31)
-- "the memorandum of understanding shall be controlling without further legislative action, except that if those provisions of a memorandum of understanding require
-- the expenditure of funds, the provisions shall not become effective unless approved by the Legislature in the annual Budget Act."
GIVEN `the holiday section is in conflict with the provisions of a memorandum of understanding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those provisions require the expenditure of funds` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Legislature has approved those provisions in the annual Budget Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the memorandum of understanding controls over Gov. Code § 6700` `the holiday section is in conflict with the provisions of a memorandum of understanding` `those provisions require the expenditure of funds` `the Legislature has approved those provisions in the annual Budget Act` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the holiday section is in conflict with the provisions of a memorandum of understanding`
            THEN REFUSE "Gov. Code § 6700(b) speaks only of a conflict between the section and the provisions of a memorandum of understanding"
        IF `those provisions require the expenditure of funds` AND NOT `the Legislature has approved those provisions in the annual Budget Act`
            THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:31 | (b) If this section is in conflict with the provisions of a memorandum of understanding reached pursuant to Chapter 12 (commencing with Section 3560) of Division 4 of Title 1, the memorandum of understanding shall be controlling without further legislative action, except that if those provisions of a memorandum of understanding require the expenditure of funds, the provisions shall not become effective unless approved by the Legislature in the annual Budget Act.
@ref Gov. Code § 6700(b) (src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:31)
GIVEN `the holiday section is in conflict with the provisions of a memorandum of understanding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those provisions require the expenditure of funds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`further legislative action is needed before the memorandum of understanding controls` `the holiday section is in conflict with the provisions of a memorandum of understanding` `those provisions require the expenditure of funds` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the holiday section is in conflict with the provisions of a memorandum of understanding`
            THEN REFUSE "Gov. Code § 6700(b) speaks only of a conflict between the section and the provisions of a memorandum of understanding"
        OTHERWISE `those provisions require the expenditure of funds`

§ `Gov. Code § 6801: January 1 is the first day of the year`

-- src:GOV-ss-6800-6808:10 | 6801. Time is computed according to the Gregorian or new style; and January 1st, in every year, after 1752 is reckoned as the first day of the year.
@ref Gov. Code § 6801 (src:GOV-ss-6800-6808:10)
-- "January 1st, in every year, after 1752 is reckoned as the first day of the year."  The text says nothing of 1752 itself or of the years before it.
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day reckoned as the first day of the year` year MEANS
    IF year GREATER THAN 1752
    THEN YMD year 1 1
    ELSE REFUSE "Gov. Code § 6801 reckons January 1 as the first day of the year in every year after 1752; it does not say which day began the year in 1752 or before"

§ `Gov. Code § 6808(a) and (c): the standard time and the power to amend`

DECLARE `Zone of standard time` IS ONE OF
    `the fifth zone designated by federal law as Pacific standard time`
    `another zone`

-- src:GOV-ss-6800-6808:24 | 6808. (a) The standard time within the state is that of the fifth zone designated by federal law as Pacific standard time (15 U.S.C. Secs. 261 and 263).
@ref Gov. Code § 6808(a) (src:GOV-ss-6800-6808:24)
GIVEN zone IS A `Zone of standard time`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the standard time within the state is that of` zone MEANS
    CONSIDER zone
    WHEN `the fifth zone designated by federal law as Pacific standard time` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `another zone` THEN FALSE

-- src:GOV-ss-6800-6808:24 | 6808. (a) The standard time within the state is that of the fifth zone designated by federal law as Pacific standard time (15 U.S.C. Secs. 261 and 263).
@ref Gov. Code § 6808(a) (src:GOV-ss-6800-6808:24)
-- The offset of Pacific standard time from Coordinated Universal Time is in 15 U.S.C. §§ 261 and 263, which the text cites and does not reproduce.
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the offset of the standard time within the state from Coordinated Universal Time in hours in the year` year MEANS
    REFUSE "Gov. Code § 6808(a) names the fifth zone designated by federal law as Pacific standard time and cites 15 U.S.C. §§ 261 and 263; the offset is in those sections, which are not deposited"

DECLARE `Kind of amendment of Gov. Code § 6808` IS ONE OF
    `a change to the dates and times of the daylight saving time period`
    `the year-round application of daylight saving time`
    `another amendment`

-- src:GOV-ss-6800-6808:26 | (c) Notwithstanding subdivision (b), the Legislature may amend this section by a two-thirds vote to change the dates and times of the daylight saving time period, consistent with federal law, and, if federal law authorizes the state to provide for the year-round application of daylight saving time, the
-- src:GOV-ss-6800-6808:27 | Legislature may amend this section by a two-thirds vote to provide for that application.
@ref Gov. Code § 6808(c) (src:GOV-ss-6800-6808:26-27)
-- "the Legislature may amend this section by a two-thirds vote to change the dates and times of the daylight saving time period, consistent with federal law, and, if federal
-- law authorizes the state to provide for the year-round application of daylight saving time, the Legislature may amend this section by a two-thirds vote to provide for that application."
-- What counts as a two-thirds vote (of which body, of the members or of those voting) is not in the deposit, so the caller says whether the vote was one.
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of amendment of Gov. Code § 6808`
      `the amendment is consistent with federal law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `federal law authorizes the state to provide for the year-round application of daylight saving time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Legislature passes the amendment by a two-thirds vote` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Gov. Code § 6808(c) lets the Legislature make the amendment` kind `the amendment is consistent with federal law` `federal law authorizes the state to provide for the year-round application of daylight saving time` `the Legislature passes the amendment by a two-thirds vote` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a change to the dates and times of the daylight saving time period`
        THEN `the amendment is consistent with federal law` AND `the Legislature passes the amendment by a two-thirds vote`
    WHEN `the year-round application of daylight saving time`
        THEN `federal law authorizes the state to provide for the year-round application of daylight saving time` AND `the Legislature passes the amendment by a two-thirds vote`
    WHEN `another amendment`
        THEN REFUSE "Gov. Code § 6808(c) says when the Legislature may amend the section to change the daylight saving time period or to provide for year-round daylight saving time; it does not say how any other amendment may be made"

§ `Gov. Code § 9606: acting in contemplation of repeal`

-- src:GOV-ss-9600-9612:25 | 9606. Any statute may be repealed at any time, except when vested rights would be impaired. Persons acting under any statute act in contemplation of this power of repeal.
@ref Gov. Code § 9606 (src:GOV-ss-9600-9612:25)
-- "Persons acting under any statute act in contemplation of this power of repeal."  The text does not say what follows from that (whether it defeats a claim of vested rights,
-- which the first sentence excepts from the power); the function states only the sentence.
GIVEN `the person acts under a statute` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person acts in contemplation of the power of repeal` `the person acts under a statute` MEANS
    `the person acts under a statute`

§ `Gov. Code § 16.5(d), (e), (f): digital and electronic signatures`

-- src:GOV-ss-1-26:72 | (d) “Digital signature” means an electronic identifier, created by computer, intended by the party using it to have the same force and effect as the use of a manual signature. For purposes of this section, a digital signature is a type of “electronic signature” as defined in subdivision (h) of Section 1633.2 of the Civil Code.
@ref Gov. Code § 16.5(d) (src:GOV-ss-1-26:72)
GIVEN `it is an electronic identifier` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is created by computer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party using it intends it to have the same force and effect as the use of a manual signature` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a digital signature in the sense of Gov. Code § 16.5(d)` `it is an electronic identifier` `it is created by computer` `the party using it intends it to have the same force and effect as the use of a manual signature` MEANS
        `it is an electronic identifier`
    AND `it is created by computer`
    AND `the party using it intends it to have the same force and effect as the use of a manual signature`

-- src:GOV-ss-1-26:72 | (d) “Digital signature” means an electronic identifier, created by computer, intended by the party using it to have the same force and effect as the use of a manual signature. For purposes of this section, a digital signature is a type of “electronic signature” as defined in subdivision (h) of Section 1633.2 of the Civil Code.
@ref Gov. Code § 16.5(d) (src:GOV-ss-1-26:72)
-- "For purposes of this section, a digital signature is a type of 'electronic signature' as defined in subdivision (h) of Section 1633.2 of the Civil Code" (not deposited).
GIVEN `it is a digital signature` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it is an electronic signature for purposes of Gov. Code § 16.5` `it is a digital signature` MEANS
    IF `it is a digital signature`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE REFUSE "Gov. Code § 16.5(d) says a digital signature is a type of electronic signature as defined in Civil Code § 1633.2(h), which is not deposited; it does not say which other things are"

-- src:GOV-ss-1-26:73 | (e) Nothing in this section shall limit the right of a public entity or government agency to use and accept an “electronic signature” as defined in subdivision (h) of Section 1633.2 of the Civil Code.
@ref Gov. Code § 16.5(e) (src:GOV-ss-1-26:73)
GIVEN `it is an electronic signature as defined in subdivision (h) of Section 1633.2 of the Civil Code` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Gov. Code § 16.5 limits the right of a public entity or government agency to use and accept it` `it is an electronic signature as defined in subdivision (h) of Section 1633.2 of the Civil Code` MEANS
    IF `it is an electronic signature as defined in subdivision (h) of Section 1633.2 of the Civil Code`
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE REFUSE "Gov. Code § 16.5(e) says nothing in the section limits the right to use and accept an electronic signature as defined in Civil Code § 1633.2(h); it does not say whether the section limits the right to use and accept anything else"

DECLARE `Kind of signature the regulations may be applied to` IS ONE OF
    `a digital signature`
    `another type of electronic signature authorized in the Uniform Electronic Transactions Act`
    `something else`

-- src:GOV-ss-1-26:74 | (f) Regulations adopted by the Secretary of State to implement this section apply only to a public entity’s use of a “digital signature” and not to use of any other type of “electronic signature” authorized in the Uniform Electronic Transactions Act (Title 2.5 (commencing with Section 1633.1) of Part 2 of Division 3 of the Civil Code).
@ref Gov. Code § 16.5(f) (src:GOV-ss-1-26:74)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of signature the regulations may be applied to`
      `it is used by a public entity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Secretary of State's regulations to implement Gov. Code § 16.5 apply to the use of` kind `it is used by a public entity` MEANS
    kind EQUALS `a digital signature` AND `it is used by a public entity`
